{"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUzNjUw","is_bot":false,"login":"macpijan","name":"Maciej Pijanowski"},"body":"**Bounty: $100**\n\nAdd new menu next to: https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-blobs/blob/main/dasharo/dasharo.ipxe#L23\n\nThat would boot from: https://boot.dasharo.com/dts/nightly.ipxe where night builds from `develop` branch land.\nNote: it must be agreed with @DaniilKl on when this nightly.ipxe leads to some functional build - if it does not rigth now.\n\nThis can be tested on QEMU.\n\nBesides checking the menu layout, one must also take care of the tests and keywords in OSFV repo.\nSpecifically:\n- https://github.com/Dasharo/open-source-firmware-validation/blob/develop/dasharo-compatibility/network-boot.robot","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM6KvrTN","author":{"login":"tlaurion"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"An idea would be to have references to latest ipxe kernel (symlinks) so that Heads could download and boot from it. Just a thought.\n\nIf those were detached signed, they coukd also be verified for integrity authr tifity prior of being kexec'ed into, without the need from Heads to use ipxe altogether.\n\nCredentials could be included in cbfs from Head side with a menu, and passed on kexec call by modifying initrd, just like heads does for tpm DUK. \n\nShould I open a seperate issue?\nThis would ease Heads upgrades from Dasharo, without needing much effort.\n\n----\n\nHow : symlinks + detached signatures needed, with base image parsing if credential file passed into cpio (heads uses secret.key) which is valid only through initramfs phase. Otherwise another mechanism to pass credentials would be needed somehow : do once and works. Could even be a file prompted by Heads to be injected as user type 50 file, only to be extracted under /tmp/secrets and wiped on boot/access to recovery shell. Simple. \n\nEx symlinks:\n\nhttps://boot.dasharo.com/dts/bzimage-latest - > https://boot.dasharo.com/dts/v2.0.0-rc5/bzImage-v2.0.0-rc5\n\nhttps://boot.dasharo.com/dts/v2.0.0-rc5/dts-base-image-latest -> https://boot.dasharo.com/dts/v2.0.0-rc5/dts-base-image-v2.0.0-rc5.cpio.gz\n\nEtc and same for detached signatures (sig/asc).\n\nHeads would point to latest files for download in ram, verify, then inject cred into reconstructed cpio then kexec into it.\n\nI can use this comment to open a referee issue if needed. I think this would be beneficial since fwupd doesn't seem to be on roadmap soon and beta testing/release would be made easy through usb tethering/rj45, easily through an option menu. ","createdAt":"2024-09-04T01:53:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-2327753933","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM66rkJm","author":{"login":"macpijan"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"@DaniilKl I wonder how relevant is this. It would be nice to have the ability to use beta versions.\n\n> That would boot from: https://boot.dasharo.com/dts/dts-rc.ipxe where releases from develop branch land.\n\nBut this seems not updated anymore. Are we going to update it, or we do not plan to?\nIf not, maybe this file should be removed?\n\nIs this effort aligned with the DTS \"nightly\" concept? Maybe we can link it here? Which .ipxe file would correspond to this nightly DTS build?","createdAt":"2025-07-29T11:15:14Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"EYES","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-3131982438","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM66sK05","author":{"login":"DaniilKl"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"@macpijan, the nightly are builds, not releases, while the RC are releases. The nightly builds (builds from `develop` branch every weekend without any testing) [will use](https://github.com/Dasharo/docs/pull/1087) [nightly.ipxe](https://boot.dasharo.com/dts/nightly.ipxe). The [dts-rc.ipxe](https://boot.dasharo.com/dts/dts-rc.ipxe) is used for RC releases that are being partially tested or not tested at all depending on the situation. We just did not need to make RC releases lately.","createdAt":"2025-07-29T11:57:20Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-3132140857","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM66sPvG","author":{"login":"DaniilKl"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"> If not, maybe this file should be removed?\n\n🤔 , deleting this means deleting our RC release workflow too. I think it should be left as is for now.","createdAt":"2025-07-29T12:02:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-3132160966","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM66sXjm","author":{"login":"macpijan"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Looking from the outside, it seems very weird that the latest release is 2.5.0, while the latest RC release is the 2.0.1-rc1. It seems this process is deleted already by simply not following it.","createdAt":"2025-07-29T12:10:40Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-3132192998","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM66sZPy","author":{"login":"macpijan"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"> The nightly builds (builds from develop branch every weekend without any testing) https://github.com/Dasharo/docs/pull/1087 [nightly.ipxe](https://boot.dasharo.com/dts/nightly.ipxe).\n\nMaybe I will transform this issue then into adding (nightly) entry.\n\nAdding (beta) entry which boots into much older RC image than the latest release, seems very much pointless.","createdAt":"2025-07-29T12:12:32Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-3132199922","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM66saU3","author":{"login":"DaniilKl"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"> Adding (beta) entry which boots into much older RC image than the latest release, seems very much pointless.\n\nI agree.","createdAt":"2025-07-29T12:13:46Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-3132204343","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM7s-sBF","author":{"login":"Houmgaor"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I'd like to claim this one with [dasharo-blobs#53](https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-blobs/pull/53). Not particularly technical, but I did full testing and validation.","createdAt":"2026-02-28T00:28:43Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-3975856197","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM7tDn6-","author":{"login":"iwanicki92"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"> But this seems not updated anymore. Are we going to update it, or we do not plan to?\n\nFixed by https://github.com/Dasharo/meta-dts/commit/3f937a1917fa68768e0726bea6c7dbc50a4fd88a (https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1754)\n`dts-rc.ipxe` will point to newest release, either `rc` or normal release.\n\n> Maybe I will transform this issue then into adding (nightly) entry.\n\nThe problem with nightly builds is that that it still uses `main` branch of https://github.com/Dasharo/dts-configs by default, while `develop` branch of meta-dts (nightly) is tested on `develop` branch of `dts-configs`.\nIt can be worked around manually, by entering shell in DTS, exporting [`DTS_CONFIG_REF`](https://github.com/Dasharo/dts-scripts/blob/4b0cc017efa7c895b9169f79f999c9278163eec6/include/dts-environment.sh#L204) variable:\n`export DTS_CONFIG_REF=refs/heads/develop` and then running DTS UI again: `dts-boot`.\nBut we might want to change this behaviour to be default one for nightly builds, especially if we want to add it to iPXE menu.","createdAt":"2026-02-28T13:12:18Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-3977150142","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM7taVyT","author":{"login":"DaniilKl"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"> But we might want to change this behaviour to be default one for nightly builds, especially if we want to add it to iPXE menu.\n\nAny ideas how to do so? The first thing that came to my mind was replasing the [DTS_CONFIG_REF value](https://github.com/Dasharo/dts-scripts/blob/4b0cc017efa7c895b9169f79f999c9278163eec6/include/dts-environment.sh#L204) via  the [dts-scripts_git.bb](https://github.com/Dasharo/meta-dts/blob/develop/meta-dts-distro/recipes-dts/dts-scripts/dts-scripts_git.bb) (e.g., by using `sed`). But I am not sure whether it is the optimal solution.","createdAt":"2026-03-02T09:15:18Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-3983105171","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM7ta4QV","author":{"login":"m-iwanicki"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Do it in Makefile if some variable is set (then set it in `EXTRA_OEMAKE` in recipe).\nOr you could maybe just add this export to `/etc/profile` so it is set by default.\n","createdAt":"2026-03-02T09:41:57Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-3983246357","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM7tghTq","author":{"login":"DaniilKl"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"> Do it in Makefile if some variable is set (then set it in `EXTRA_OEMAKE` in recipe). Or you could maybe just add this export to `/etc/profile` so it is set by default.\n\nI agree with the propositions. Then we need to trigger it during Yocto build somehow. We can either do it by passing some variable to kas either by `export The_VARIABLE ...; kas-container` or modifying some `kas/*.yml` file using, for example, `sed` in CI. Or we can add a separate YAML file (for example `kas-develop.yml`) that will be used for building from `develop` branch.","createdAt":"2026-03-02T14:25:27Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-3984725226","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM7tmbPU","author":{"login":"yuliuyi717-ux"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I can take this bounty. Plan:\n1) add the new Nightly menu entry in dasharo-blobs () next to the existing DTS entry\n2) point it to  behind a build-time toggle so it can be safely enabled\n3) update OSFV network boot test/keywords to validate the new menu entry path\n4) verify on QEMU and post test evidence in the PR\n\nI’ll split this into focused commits so review is straightforward.","createdAt":"2026-03-02T19:01:38Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-3986273236","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM7tmbcq","author":{"login":"yuliuyi717-ux"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Correction to my previous comment (some inline code got stripped):\n\n1) add the new Nightly menu entry in dasharo-blobs (`dasharo/dasharo.ipxe`) next to the existing DTS entry\n2) point it to `https://boot.dasharo.com/dts/nightly.ipxe` behind a build-time toggle so it can be safely enabled\n3) update OSFV network boot test/keywords to validate the new menu entry path\n4) verify on QEMU and post test evidence in the PR\n\nI will proceed with this plan.","createdAt":"2026-03-02T19:01:49Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-3986274090","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM7tmkka","author":{"login":"yuliuyi717-ux"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Update: I submitted the implementation in two focused PRs so review can happen per repo:\n\n1) Dasharo/dasharo-blobs#54\n- adds `Dasharo Tools Suite (Nightly)` to `dasharo.ipxe`\n- chains to `https://boot.dasharo.com/dts/nightly.ipxe`\n\n2) Dasharo/open-source-firmware-validation#1252\n- updates `network-boot.robot` menu-order checks for the new entry\n- adds a dedicated nightly boot validation test (`PXE004.002`)\n\nBoth PRs are linked to this issue and ready for review.","createdAt":"2026-03-02T19:09:41Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-3986311450","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM7zDoh4","author":{"login":"redwing509"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #1041\n\nImplementation plan:\n1. Analyze the existing codebase and understand the requirements\n2. Implement the requested changes with clean, tested code\n3. Add comprehensive tests covering the acceptance criteria\n4. Submit PR with documentation updates if needed\n\nEstimated delivery: within 24 hours.","createdAt":"2026-03-17T20:29:29Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-4077815928","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM7zD6Wg","author":{"login":"yuliuyi717-ux"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"For clarity, this issue is already covered on my side by the two linked PRs submitted on March 2:\n\n- Dasharo/dasharo-blobs#54 — adds the `Dasharo Tools Suite (Nightly)` menu entry and chains to `https://boot.dasharo.com/dts/nightly.ipxe`\n- Dasharo/open-source-firmware-validation#1252 — updates the OSFV network boot checks for the new menu layout and adds dedicated coverage for the Nightly DTS path\n\nThat split follows the issue scope directly: one PR for the iPXE menu entry, and one PR for the OSFV test updates mentioned in the bounty description.\n\nIf it helps review, I can also add a compact validation summary to either PR, but from an implementation standpoint the requested work for #1041 is already submitted and ready for review.\n","createdAt":"2026-03-17T20:41:50Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-4077888928","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOEtsrhM8AAAABDASu0g","author":{"login":"Spina7"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Opened PRs for this bounty:\\n\\n- dasharo-blobs: https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-blobs/pull/57\\n- OSFV tests/keywords: https://github.com/Dasharo/open-source-firmware-validation/pull/1271\\n\\nThe nightly endpoint currently returns 200 OK, and both PR bodies include local verification.","createdAt":"2026-05-20T09:13:57Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041#issuecomment-4496600786","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"createdAt":"2024-09-03T21:26:14Z","labels":[{"id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNTM3MjIxMzY0","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"},{"id":"LA_kwDOEtsrhM8AAAACAUsYBg","name":"bounty-easy","description":"","color":"aaaaaa"}],"state":"OPEN","title":"Add \"Dasharo Tools Suite (Nightly)\" to iPXE menu entry","updatedAt":"2026-05-20T09:33:57Z","url":"https://github.com/Dasharo/dasharo-issues/issues/1041"}
